{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019rxTZhy8AFqtaHsQv6Njro","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven development experiment using classic Unix utilities as a test bed. It derives formal specs from C source code, generates Go implementations via an AI orchestrator, and verifies parity against GNU reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify) with `cmd/` per-utility packages, `pkg/sys/` for syscall abstractions, `pkg/format/` for output formatting, `pkg/testutils/` for the differential testing harness, and `magefiles/` for build orchestration.\n\n**Current implementation state** (from source_code, which takes precedence over documentation):\n- **Complete with code + tests**: pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/cat, cmd/du, cmd/false, cmd/ls, cmd/sponge, cmd/true, cmd/wc\n- **Code exists, no tests**: cmd/version\n- **No code**: cmd/yes, cmd/basename, cmd/dirname (release 02.0, specs pending), cmd/tee (release 02.1, specs pending), cmd/head, cmd/seq (release 02.2, specs pending)\n- **Spec complete, code extension needed**: rel04.1 ls-extended\n\n**Current release priority**: Release 00.0 is the earliest release with a gap — `rel00.0-uc001-magefiles` includes `cmd/version` as its only code generation target (per DD7), and `cmd/version/main.go` exists but has no test file. All other release 00.0 use cases (format, sys, testutils) are complete with tests.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 00.0 is the earliest incomplete release. The sole gap is `cmd/version` lacking tests. This blocks declaring rel00.0 complete. Releases 02.0–02.2 have pending specs (no PRDs for yes/basename/dirname/tee/head/seq), so code tasks cannot be anchored to PRD requirements. Release 04.1 (ls-extended) has complete specs but is much later in priority order.\n\nThe `cmd/version` test task is anchored to prd011-magefiles R1.1, R1.2, R1.4 — three PRD sub-requirements with clear, testable behavior. The utility is simple (print version string, exit 0) and the test file follows established patterns from cmd/true and cmd/false.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd011-magefiles R1.1, R1.2, R1.4: cmd/version unit tests\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - cmd/version/main.go (existing implementation to test)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd011-magefiles.yaml (PRD requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.4)\n      - cmd/true/true_test.go (TestMain pattern -- binary compilation to temp dir, subprocess execution, cleanup)\n      - cmd/false/false_test.go (test structure for simple utilities without differential reference)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/version/version_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Unit tests for version command covering output format, default version value, and flag handling\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test prd011-magefiles R1.1: running the version binary with no arguments prints the version string to stdout followed by a newline and exits with code 0\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test prd011-magefiles R1.2: when built without -ldflags setting main.version, the output is exactly the string 'dev' followed by a newline\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test prd011-magefiles R1.4: the --version flag prints the version string to stdout and exits 0, and the -v flag produces identical output to --version\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Verify that all valid invocations (no args, --version, -v) produce no output on stderr\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Implement TestMain that builds the version binary into a temp directory using go build and cleans up after all tests complete\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use direct subprocess execution via os/exec to run the compiled binary and check stdout, stderr, and exit code. Do not use differential testing (pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests) because cmd/version has no GNU reference binary -- it is a project-specific command, not a re-implementation of a Unix utility.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Follow the TestMain pattern from cmd/true/true_test.go: create a temp directory with os.MkdirTemp, compile the binary with exec.Command('go', 'build', '-o', goBinary, '.'), store the path in a package-level var goBinary, run m.Run(), and os.RemoveAll the temp directory on exit.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Use package main (not package main_test) matching the convention in all other cmd/ test files. Include the standard copyright header: '// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.' and '// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT'.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/version/version_test.go exists and compiles with go vet ./cmd/version/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/version/ passes with all tests green\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"A test named TestVersionNoArgs verifies that running the binary with no arguments outputs exactly 'dev\\\\n' to stdout, produces empty stderr, and exits with code 0\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"A test named TestVersionFlags verifies that --version and -v each produce stdout output identical to the no-args invocation, with empty stderr and exit code 0\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"TestMain compiles the binary successfully and cleans up the temp directory after tests complete\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":96062,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":96062},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1afe0577-f091-4365-92d5-4f002678a00c","uuid":"91905ac3-35b5-4776-a46